 Anduril Intelligence Systems (AIS) is focused on positioning Anduril as a lead provider of specialized engineering and products for Intelligence Community (IC) customers. We work within the IC to understand their requirements, shape their concepts of operation, and deliver exquisite capability across their problem set. We aim to develop and deploy critically needed capabilities that address our customers’ most pressing national security requirements. &nbsp; 

 ABOUT THE JOB &nbsp; 

 We are looking for a Electrical Product Sustainment Engineer to join our rapidly growing team in Costa Mesa, California. In this role, you will keep our production operations running smoothly once products are in the field and on the line. You will triage product failures, drive root cause investigations to closure through process or design updates, and manage failure and field data to understand population-level impact. You will work cross-functionally with Quality, Supply Chain, and Production Operations to keep builds on plan and surface any issues that threaten the build schedule. Your work directly ensures that the capabilities our customers depend on are delivered reliably and at scale, sustaining fielded systems long after they leave the line. This is a high-impact, hands-on role for an engineer who thrives on solving hard problems quickly and turning production challenges into lasting design and process improvements. &nbsp; 

 WHAT YOU’LL DO &nbsp; 


 Triage product failures from production and the field, prioritizing by severity and population impact 

 Drive root cause investigations down to the electrical component and PCB fabrication level as needed, landing corrective actions as process or design updates

 Collect, manage, and analyze failure and field data to quantify population-level impact and trends

 Work cross-functionally with Quality, Supply Chain, and Production Operations to keep builds on plan

 Surface and escalate issues that threaten the build schedule, and drive them to resolution

 Implement design and process changes that improve yield, reliability, and manufacturability

 Evaluate supplier product change notifications (PCNs) and assess their impact to the production environment, partnering with the design team to update the design as needed

 Support production test, debug, and failure analysis at the board and system level

 Track and report on sustainment metrics, corrective action status, and open production issues

 Work in a fast-paced environment, having to juggle multiple concurrent projects and customers &nbsp; 


 REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; 


 Currently possesses and is able to maintain an active U.S. Secret security clearance 

 1-3+ years of professional experience in hardware product development, sustainment, or manufacturing engineering

 Experience with root cause analysis and structured problem-solving methods (e.g., 8D, 5 Whys, fishbone, FMEA)

 Deep understanding of fabrication and assembly-level failure analysis methods, including CT scan, X-ray, visual inspection, cross-sectioning, and SEM image analysis

 Ability to read and interpret schematics and apply best practices appropriate for each design

 Familiarity with standard interfaces such as Ethernet, CAN, I2C, SPI, PCIe, and USB

 Proficiency with data analysis tools to track failure trends and quantify population impact (e.g., Excel, SQL, Python, JMP)

 Knowledge of modern analog and digital electronics and electronic circuits

 Ability to determine work priorities based on broad direction from management

 Experience working cross-functionally with Quality, Supply Chain, and Production Operations in a manufacturing environment


 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; 


 Understanding of MIL-STD-810 and relevant military environmental qualification standards 

 Understanding of MIL-STD-461 and relevant military electromagnetic compatibility standards

 Experience with PLM/ERP systems and managing engineering change orders (ECOs)

 Familiarity with production quality systems, CAPA processes, and statistical process control (SPC) &nbsp; 

