 Program and operate metrology equipment across contact and non-contact systems to validate that parts meet requirements. &nbsp; 



 Write, debug, and optimize inspection programs to improve accuracy, repeatability, and cycle time. &nbsp; 



 Troubleshoot complex measurement issues — determining why an inspection is failing or producing inconsistent results — and resolve process-level problems. &nbsp; 



 Design, build, and validate holding fixtures used on the CMMs. &nbsp; 



 Work closely with the Quality Engineering team to support problem-solving, root cause analysis, and product design. &nbsp; 



 Define best-practice inspection and reporting strategies with cross-functional teams. &nbsp; 



 Maintain and improve lab equipment and processes (calibration, cleanliness, best practices), reducing downtime and ensuring data reliability. &nbsp; 



 Train and mentor other metrology team members and serve as the go-to resource for difficult measurement problems. &nbsp; 



 Help ensure compliance with industry standards (e.g., AS9100, ISO 17025). &nbsp; 


