 5+ years of metrology experience, including programming CMMs. &nbsp; 



 Hands-on experience with at least three different types of metrology equipment (CNC CMM, portable CMM, laser tracker, large-volume or automated 3D scanners, optical comparator, etc.). &nbsp; 



 Proficiency with CMM software; Calypso or Polyworks preferred (PC-DMIS, Verisurf, MCosmos, or equivalent acceptable with the ability to learn PolyWorks and Calypso quickly). &nbsp; 



 Excellent understanding of GD&amp;T (ASME Y14.5). &nbsp; 



 Experience designing and building holding fixtures for CMMs. &nbsp; 



 Proficiency with precision measuring equipment (micrometers, height gauges, and other hand tools). &nbsp; 



 Strong analytical skills, attention to detail, and excellent communication skills. &nbsp; 



 Ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. security clearance. &nbsp; 


 &nbsp; 

 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; 


 Associate’s degree or technical training. &nbsp; 



 Experience with advanced or specialized inspection methods, including NDT. &nbsp; 



 Experience with CT scanning and automated or large-volume 3D scanning. &nbsp; 



 Experience with PolyWorks|DataLoop or similar metrology data management platforms. &nbsp; 



 Familiarity with AS9100 or ISO 17025 quality systems. &nbsp; 

