 &nbsp;

 WHAT YOU’LL DO &nbsp; 


 Own the thermal design and analysis of a space vehicle or payload program &nbsp; 



 Use first principles as a basis for every decision and discern the right level of analysis to apply. Execute hand calculations, spreadsheet, and MATLAB/Python first-order models to inform path forward before jumping into detailed design &nbsp; 



 Define worst case thermal environments across the vehicle mission lifetime &nbsp; 



 Define system thermal budgets and requirements through collaboration with engineers in other disciplines &nbsp; 



 Drive thermal architectures and hardware definitions, such as radiator sizing, coating selections, heater power allocation, MLI definitions, thermal interface material selections, thermal management techniques, and trading heat transport devices &nbsp; 



 Support PCBA thermal analysis and electronic component thermal management &nbsp; 



 Own the development, planning, and execution of unit and system thermal vacuum, thermal balance, and thermal cycle tests &nbsp; 



 Develop internal tools to improve the effectiveness and efficiency of analysis &nbsp; 



 Develop, prepare, and execute thermal tests to inform analysis and reduce risk on key hardware assemblies &nbsp; 


