 BS, MS, or higher degree in engineering, applied physics, or hard science &nbsp; 



 Demonstrated knowledge of heat transfer in academic and/or professional setting&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Application of first-order hand calculations to drive thermal architectures and verify accuracy of higher fidelity models &nbsp; 



 Proficiency in Thermal Desktop or equivalent thermal simulation tool &nbsp; 



 Thermal experience with spacecraft components such as optical payloads, electronics, mechanisms, etc. &nbsp; 



 Hands-on experience prototyping hardware and conducting thermal tests&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience with CAD, selecting instrumentation, post-processing data, correlating models &nbsp; 



 Ability to independently navigate and solve complex, open-ended technical problems in a fast-paced environment &nbsp; 



 CAD experience (Siemens NX preferred) &nbsp; 



 Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to communicate pros/cons of system architecture with respect to thermal considerations &nbsp; 



 Passion for defending the United States and her allies &nbsp; 



 U.S. Person status is required as this position needs to access export-controlled data &nbsp; 


 &nbsp;

 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; 


 Highly proficient using Thermal Desktop (3+ years) &nbsp; 



 Design or test experience on a space platform &nbsp; 



 Experience developing code in higher-level languages like Python or MATLAB for applications like lumped thermal capacitance steady state and transient analysis &nbsp; 



 Experience with full life cycle of space hardware development, from concept to on-orbit operation &nbsp; 



 Experience using FloCAD and SINDA/FLUINT &nbsp; 



 Experience with driving implementation of passive and active thermal control hardware &nbsp; 



 Be able to obtain and hold a U.S. Top Secret security clearance &nbsp; 

