 The Air Defense team builds robots that find other robots and knock them out of the sky. At a time when air superiority can no longer be taken for granted, the Air Defense team provides mission critical capabilities to warfighters. From detection to tracking, identification, deterrence, and defeat, our family of networked sensors and effectors enables our customers to rapidly close the kill chain against a broad range of UAS threats. Working across product, engineering, business development, logistics, operations, and mission success, the Air Defense team develops, tests, deploys, and sustains the Anduril Air Defense Family of Systems in challenging operational environments worldwide.

 ABOUT THE ROLE

 We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced SW Release Manager. In this critical role, you will define and manage major software releases aligned with program milestones, delivering production-quality software for safety and mission-critical systems across multiple product variants. You will be instrumental in ensuring timely, secure, and reliable software delivery to our customers and warfighters. &nbsp; 

 &nbsp;WHAT YOU'LL DO &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;Work closely with System Engineers and Product teams&nbsp;to translate software requirements into release plans and deliverables. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;Ensure timely delivery of software releases artifacts including&nbsp;any&nbsp;supporting documentation. &nbsp; 

 * Continuously improve the processes in support of release and quality improvement. &nbsp; 

 * Manage and coordinate the deployment of development releases to test and evaluation teams for validation. &nbsp; 

 * Implement and manage automated testing and deployment processes in an established continuous integration/continuous delivery (CI/CD) environment. &nbsp; 

 * Utilize Git and CI automations to execute nightly and automated builds and system checks. &nbsp; 

 * Define and develop software-in-the-loop (SITL) and hardware-in-the-loop (HITL) tests to validate system-level performance and assure system quality. &nbsp; 

 Required Qualifications: &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience owning a software release process. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with software build automation tooling such as GitHub, CircleCI, and other DevOps relevant tools. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Proven track record of managing the deployment of production software and interacting with CI/CD pipelines. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Strong coding skills and a background in applying automated test coverage infrastructure (on-device and in the cloud). &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Past experience&nbsp;in at least one of C++, Rust, or Go, and proficiency in Python and Bash&nbsp;/ Command Line&nbsp;scripting. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Familiarity with the Department of Defense (DoD) ecosystem for the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC), (e.g.,&nbsp;MIL-STD-882 for System Safety Engineering, Security Technical Implementation Guides (STIGs), DevSecOps best practices for continuous ATO). &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ability to&nbsp;present strategic, technical, and operational updates to&nbsp;stakeholders at&nbsp;all levels&nbsp; &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; U.S. Person status is required as this position needs to access&nbsp;export-controlled&nbsp;data. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Must be eligible to obtain and hold a US DoD Security Clearance. &nbsp; 

 Preferred Qualifications: &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with Nix/NixOS. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Proven experience&nbsp;in an Engineering role, demonstrating leadership and innovation. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience&nbsp;with both&nbsp;edge&nbsp;and cloud deployments &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience implementing automated testing frameworks in software-in-the-loop (SITL) and hardware-in-the-loop (HITL) environments. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience in Agile methodologies. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with Unix/Linux tools for performance analysis and debugging problems (e.g., valgrind, perf). &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Solid understanding of systems software (kernel, device drivers, system calls). &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience working with networked sensor modules via Ethernet/CAN/Serial and using interface specifications or protocols to collect and analyze data. &nbsp; 

 *&nbsp;&nbsp; Ability to travel up to&nbsp;25% time. &nbsp; 
