 Proven experience establishing technical standards or specifications for hardware programs &nbsp; 



 Strong foundation in materials science principles, including material properties, surface chemistry, and contamination mechanisms &nbsp; 



 Demonstrated ability to design experiments, analyze data, and draw defensible engineering conclusions &nbsp; 



 Self-directed work style with ability to define scope for ambiguous problems &nbsp; 



 U.S. citizenship required &nbsp; 


 &nbsp;

 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; 


 Knowledge of manufacturing processes (bonding, heat treating, machining, coating, surface finishing, welding, composites, soldering, etc.) &nbsp; 



 Experience with contamination control and/or EEE parts selection and PCBA materials (manufacturing, acceptability, failure analysis) is highly desired.&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 For candidates with contamination control experience the following are desired: &nbsp; 



 Intimate familiarity with cleanroom classification levels, best practices, and operations &nbsp; 



 Hands-on experience with spacecraft contamination control&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience with outgassing characterization (ASTM E595, ASTM E1559)&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 For candidates with EEE parts selection and printed circuit board assembly experience the following are desired: &nbsp; 



 Experience with EEE parts qualification and destructive physical analysis (DPA) &nbsp; 



 Knowledge of manufacturing processes (PCB manufacturing, PCB assembly) &nbsp; 



 Experience with conformal coating selection, application processes and inspection&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Prior electronic failure analysis experience &nbsp; 



 Experience with contamination modeling tools &nbsp; 



 Proficiency in interpreting data from different material characterization techniques (FTIR, SEM, TGA, etc.) &nbsp; 



 Understanding of space environment effects (charged particle radiation, UV exposure, atomic oxygen) &nbsp; 



 Experience in adjacent high-reliability industries (aerospace, defense, semiconductor, medical devices) &nbsp; 



 Experience with contamination control for precision optics or infrared sensor systems &nbsp; 



 Experience with statistical analysis tools and design of experiments (DOE) &nbsp; 


