 ABOUT THE ROLE &nbsp; 

 Anduril is seeking a Senior Mechanical Engineer specializing in electromechanical packaging and sensor integration to design, test, and scale mission-critical hardware&nbsp; across our autonomous air, sea, ground, and strike platforms. &nbsp; 

 WHAT YOU’LL DO &nbsp; 


 Own enclosures, sensor integration, and electromechanical assemblies fro m requirements definition, hand calculations, and conceptual design through prototyping, testing, and volume manufacturing. &nbsp; 

 Create high-fidelity 3D models and fully defined 2D drawing packages &nbsp; 

 Design parts across diverse fabrication processes including designs for injection/other molding, precision 3/5-axis CNC machining, complex weldments, sheet metal, composite layups, and structural adhesive bonding. &nbsp; 

 Apply first-principles engineering and FEA/hand calculations to validate structural, thermal, and vibrational performance under harsh operational and environmental conditions. &nbsp; 

 Perform 1D/3D tolerance stacks, DFMEAs, and tool-access assessments early in development to de-risk production bottlenecks and scale throughput. &nbsp; 

 Build physical prototypes, author detailed test plans, and run functional testing (environmental, dynamic, bench-top, or live arena/range tests depending on track). &nbsp; 

 Collaborate with Electrical, Systems, Mechanical, Manufacturing, Quality, Safety, and Test teams, as well as external suppliers, to solve urgent hardware bottlenecks. &nbsp; 


 REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; 


 Bachelor's, Master’s, or PhD degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, or a related discipline. &nbsp; 

 4+ years of professional mechanical design experience taking physical hardware from initial concept through fabrication and functional test or LRIP. &nbsp; 

 Proficiency in parametric 3D CAD (NX preferred, SolidWorks, or Creo) and modern PLM/PDM environments (e.g., Teamcenter). &nbsp; 

 Working knowledge of engineering drawings and practical application of ASME Y14.5 GD&amp;T and tolerance stack-up analysis. &nbsp; 

 Hands-on prototyping and fabrication experience, including root-cause analysis of manufacturing and hardware defects. &nbsp; 

 Professional experience applying statics, dynamics, material selection, heat transfer, and structural mechanics to hardware design problems. &nbsp; 

 Experience designing hardware with Design for Manufacturability and Assembly (DFM/DFA) in mind for future volume production (e.g., fast-paced automotive, robotics, aerospace, or marine environments). &nbsp; 

 Experience designing tightly integrated electromechanical systems (dense PCBA packaging, active/passive thermal management, RF/EMI shielding, harness routing, and environmental sealing / IP ratings). &nbsp; 

 Prior experience in defense, maritime, optics, automotive, or other highly regulated hardware development environments. &nbsp; 

 Eligible for U.S. Security Clearance (DoD Secret, Top Secret, or DOE Q) &nbsp; 

 Up to 15% travel &nbsp; 


 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; 


 Proficiency with FEA tools (Abaqus, ANSYS, or equivalent) for structural, thermal, or dynamic analysis. &nbsp; 

 Deep expertise in tooling design, high-volume injection molding, robotic/manual weldment design, structural bonding, or building visual standard operating procedures (SOPs). &nbsp; 

 Familiarity with ECAD tools (e.g., Altium Designer) or basic PCB design / schematic review. &nbsp; 


